WEBVTT

00:09.843 --> 00:13.054
The most important
is the balance of the body.

00:13.805 --> 00:15.473
It's the legs and hips.

00:16.266 --> 00:19.769
Balancing our body
with strong legs and hips

00:19.853 --> 00:23.857
leads to accurate attacks
and solid defense.

00:24.733 --> 00:28.361
First, a training to withstand
under the waterfall.

00:28.445 --> 00:30.155
I'm gonna die!

00:30.864 --> 00:34.117
Next, carry three logs.

00:34.200 --> 00:35.577
So thick.

00:36.411 --> 00:41.124
Lastly, push and move this boulder
one cho.

00:41.708 --> 00:43.418
ONE CHO IS ABOUT 109 METERS

00:43.960 --> 00:48.089
My training consists of
just these three simple tasks.

00:49.174 --> 00:53.052
Burning you with fire from below
is dangerous, so we'll skip that.

00:53.136 --> 00:55.096
Sorry!

00:55.180 --> 00:57.223
Zenitsu passed out!

00:58.349 --> 00:59.934
Put him in the river.

01:01.352 --> 01:04.898
To you who is ignorant of
What eternity means

01:04.981 --> 01:08.193
It's time to show you the answer

01:08.276 --> 01:14.574
Beyond the endless spiral

01:23.249 --> 01:28.046
DEMON SLAYER: KIMETSU NO YAIBA:
HASHIRA TRAINING ARC

01:30.381 --> 01:33.802
The reason why it sounded like an excuse

01:33.885 --> 01:37.347
A weakness that draws in a fleeting future

01:37.430 --> 01:42.560
You mistake it for strength

01:43.937 --> 01:45.772
So detestable, so detestable

01:45.855 --> 01:47.774
So disgraceful, so disgraceful

01:47.857 --> 01:50.902
The heart that is so bleak

01:50.985 --> 01:52.779
So dark, so dark

01:52.862 --> 01:54.739
That it almost hides the moon

01:54.823 --> 01:58.326
If only you weren't here

01:58.409 --> 02:01.913
It sways and sways

02:01.996 --> 02:05.542
Carrying on its intentions
Just like a flower

02:05.625 --> 02:08.920
Taking it all away, taking it all away

02:09.003 --> 02:12.423
It tears the heart just like a storm would

02:12.507 --> 02:16.010
To you who is ignorant of
What eternity means

02:16.094 --> 02:19.556
It's time to show you the answer

02:19.639 --> 02:24.936
Beyond the endless spiral

02:25.019 --> 02:29.149
Who awaits there

02:32.235 --> 02:36.948
EPISODE 6: THE STRONGEST IN
THE DEMON SLAYER CORPS

02:41.953 --> 02:43.997
It's so cold!

02:44.080 --> 02:47.834
The river in winter is way too cold!

02:47.917 --> 02:49.836
I could die! I feel like throwing up!

02:49.919 --> 02:51.921
-Zenitsu!
-Land! Land!

02:52.005 --> 02:54.465
My internal organs hurt!
They're screaming!

02:54.549 --> 02:56.426
They're saying I'm going to die!

02:59.137 --> 03:01.556
It's no use! Too late!
I got out of the water!

03:01.639 --> 03:03.391
But I'm gonna freeze to death!

03:07.896 --> 03:10.148
Long time no see, you both.

03:10.940 --> 03:13.192
Here, cling to the rocks.

03:13.276 --> 03:14.903
They're warm.

03:19.991 --> 03:22.285
It's… so warm.

03:22.368 --> 03:24.704
Are rocks this warm?

03:24.787 --> 03:27.916
It feels like being in my mother's arms.

03:30.001 --> 03:32.629
Mommy!

03:33.379 --> 03:35.256
Mommy!

03:37.634 --> 03:40.428
So cold. This is harsh.

03:40.511 --> 03:43.014
Waterfall training is brutal.

03:44.057 --> 03:49.646
Boar Rush. Boar Rush.
Boar Rush. Boar Rush.

03:49.729 --> 03:53.274
-Namu Amida… I can't!
-Boar Rush. Boar Rush.

03:53.900 --> 03:56.903
Inosuke is doing his best too.
I must not lose.

04:00.448 --> 04:02.283
His chanting stopped?

04:03.076 --> 04:05.245
Huh? Inosuke?

04:05.328 --> 04:07.038
Oh, no! This is bad!

04:07.121 --> 04:10.166
Inosuke! Wake up, Inosuke!
Come back to life!

04:10.250 --> 04:12.877
Inosuke, please get up!

04:13.920 --> 04:15.630
You called, Manjiro?

04:15.713 --> 04:18.716
Inosuke!

04:18.883 --> 04:20.802
Boar Rush…

04:21.636 --> 04:23.388
This waterfall…

04:24.973 --> 04:26.724
is really something else.

04:26.808 --> 04:29.811
Keep chanting Nembutsu without stopping.

04:29.894 --> 04:32.063
It's to help you stay focused,

04:32.146 --> 04:35.441
but also to signal
that you're still conscious.

04:36.150 --> 04:37.443
Okay.

04:37.527 --> 04:39.070
Namu Amida Butsu…

04:39.779 --> 04:43.157
The water is cold, and it hits hard.

04:43.241 --> 04:44.993
I must not keep quiet.

04:45.076 --> 04:47.078
Nembutsu… Nembutsu…

04:47.161 --> 04:51.541
-Namu Amida Butsu…
-Nembutsu… Nembutsu…

04:51.624 --> 04:56.713
Nembutsu… Nembutsu…

04:57.922 --> 04:59.507
So cold!

05:01.926 --> 05:05.805
Just getting hit by the waterfall
felt really painful.

05:05.888 --> 05:09.809
I never thought water falling
from such a height could be so heavy.

05:09.892 --> 05:13.021
If I relax my body,
it feels like my neck might break.

05:13.104 --> 05:16.482
No, no. You and that Boar Head
are amazing.

05:16.566 --> 05:20.570
It took me until evening to stay
under the waterfall on my first day.

05:20.653 --> 05:22.405
It's hard to get used to the water.

05:22.488 --> 05:26.242
Since I've managed to withstand
being hit by the waterfall,

05:26.326 --> 05:28.870
I'm moving on to carrying the logs.

05:28.953 --> 05:32.332
Wow. You're incredible, Murata.

05:32.415 --> 05:35.418
Well, I've been here for ten days.

05:43.301 --> 05:46.262
That Prayer Beads-Rattling Guy is amazing.

05:46.345 --> 05:48.848
That's the Stone Hashira,
his name is Himejima.

05:48.931 --> 05:51.267
Don't give him strange nicknames.

05:51.350 --> 05:54.562
I was startled the first time I met him.

05:54.645 --> 05:56.773
You eat the bones too, Inosuke?

05:56.856 --> 06:00.318
Yeah. You don't?
They're crunchy and delicious.

06:00.401 --> 06:01.527
Wow!

06:01.611 --> 06:06.157
Out of all the people I know,
you eat fish the cleanest.

06:06.240 --> 06:10.036
I'm King of The Mountains after all!
I'm the best at everything!

06:10.119 --> 06:11.454
That's natural!

06:11.537 --> 06:15.083
You still want to eat?
You're already on your tenth.

06:15.166 --> 06:18.753
About that Prayer Beads-Rattling Guy.

06:18.836 --> 06:21.422
Himejima the Stone Hashira, remember?

06:22.215 --> 06:26.928
Without a doubt, he is the strongest
in the Demon Slayer Corps.

06:27.011 --> 06:29.180
Oh, you think so too?

06:29.263 --> 06:31.057
-Huh?
-Is that so?

06:31.140 --> 06:34.310
Himejima smells completely different
from the others.

06:34.393 --> 06:36.896
I wonder if he's already
manifested his mark.

06:36.979 --> 06:39.482
If he did, I wouldn't be surprised.

06:39.565 --> 06:44.362
I can't keep up with the talk of people
who rise in rank in such a short time.

06:44.445 --> 06:46.864
Normally, you wouldn't understand that.

06:46.948 --> 06:48.991
They're on a different level.

06:49.075 --> 06:51.828
Also, Tanjiro's grilled fish is delicious.

06:51.911 --> 06:53.830
I don't believe it.

06:54.622 --> 06:58.960
I bet that Old Guy can't even
move the boulder one cho.

06:59.043 --> 07:01.379
He's just enjoying bullying the newcomers.

07:01.462 --> 07:06.592
You're wrong. Himejima can push
an even bigger boulder than that.

07:06.676 --> 07:09.303
You believe everything you're told?

07:09.387 --> 07:10.888
You're being deceived.

07:10.972 --> 07:12.348
Of course not.

07:12.432 --> 07:14.725
You have good hearing.

07:14.809 --> 07:18.396
You should be able to tell
if someone's lying or not, right?

07:20.440 --> 07:23.860
Namu Amida Butsu. Namu Amida Butsu.

07:23.943 --> 07:26.279
Oh, he's here.

07:28.781 --> 07:31.409
Himejima is really amazing!

07:31.492 --> 07:33.703
Can I become like him?

07:33.786 --> 07:37.457
No way in hell!

07:37.540 --> 07:39.041
Are you dumb?

07:39.125 --> 07:41.794
Hello? Is your head okay?

07:42.628 --> 07:46.132
That Old Guy is abnormal!
He's huge like a bear, to begin with!

07:46.215 --> 07:47.550
Well, but--

07:47.633 --> 07:48.634
Shut up!

07:48.718 --> 07:51.596
There's a natural gap
between giants and dwarfs!

07:51.679 --> 07:53.347
You know what I mean!

07:53.431 --> 07:55.558
Now I'm full.

07:55.641 --> 07:57.852
I'm gonna carry the logs
and push the boulder.

07:57.935 --> 07:59.937
Dang! Why are you so positive?

08:00.021 --> 08:01.689
There's no place for me!

08:01.772 --> 08:02.899
Calm down.

08:02.982 --> 08:04.066
Here I go!

08:04.150 --> 08:05.443
Calm down.

08:05.526 --> 08:10.990
-Nembutsu! Nembutsu! Nembutsu!
-Namu Amida Butsu! Namu Amida Butsu!

08:11.073 --> 08:12.158
-Zenitsu!
-Namu…

08:16.078 --> 08:17.663
Zenitsu!

08:17.747 --> 08:20.708
Namu Amida Butsu! Namu Amida Butsu!
Namu Amida…

08:27.340 --> 08:30.092
Waterfall training, complete.

08:42.396 --> 08:45.358
Carrying the logs, complete.

08:47.693 --> 08:50.363
Finally, the last one.

09:09.465 --> 09:11.092
SLAY

09:13.302 --> 09:16.180
FOUR

09:16.264 --> 09:19.183
I found another one.

09:19.267 --> 09:24.313
Now I've located about 60%
of the demon hunters.

09:25.189 --> 09:30.027
But I haven't found the girl
who overcame the sun.

09:31.028 --> 09:36.742
Nakime, you've grown more than I thought.

09:37.910 --> 09:39.412
How wonderful.

09:50.756 --> 09:56.470
Nakime, you've grown more than I thought.

09:57.513 --> 09:58.848
How wonderful.

09:59.515 --> 10:01.475
It is an honor.

10:02.435 --> 10:04.353
Next, let's see…

10:05.605 --> 10:06.897
Check around here.

10:07.773 --> 10:09.317
As you wish.

10:25.249 --> 10:27.585
Found more of them.

10:28.586 --> 10:31.130
Keep tailing them.

10:31.839 --> 10:33.674
As you wish.

10:43.893 --> 10:49.148
I will find Nezuko and Ubuyashiki soon.

10:58.366 --> 11:00.534
My feet keep sliding back!

11:01.535 --> 11:03.204
I can't push the boulder!

11:12.129 --> 11:13.422
Ouch!

11:16.258 --> 11:18.552
I guess I'll head back to get this fixed.

11:21.013 --> 11:22.556
Good morning!

11:22.640 --> 11:24.141
Oh, Kamado.

11:25.309 --> 11:28.813
We're going to get down off the mountain.
We just can't keep up.

11:30.523 --> 11:34.276
Sorry. It pains our hearts
to withdraw from here, but…

11:34.777 --> 11:38.030
But we'll provide backup support
for you from behind.

11:39.198 --> 11:41.158
We're counting on you, Kamado.

11:42.743 --> 11:45.162
Okay, then. I'm counting on you as well.

11:47.373 --> 11:48.833
Huh? You're counting on us?

11:49.667 --> 11:54.130
If you all support us from behind,
we can focus on fighting the demons.

11:55.089 --> 11:59.176
Let's use the strength of all the Corps
to sever Muzan Kibutsuji's head!

12:00.803 --> 12:03.055
Got it. Leave the rear to us.

12:03.139 --> 12:04.348
Roger that, Kamado.

12:04.432 --> 12:05.683
You can count on us.

12:10.813 --> 12:14.358
And I have my own duty.

12:21.907 --> 12:25.244
Wow! Tanjiro, you're really good
at making onigiris.

12:25.327 --> 12:27.538
Totally! They're perfectly triangular.

12:27.621 --> 12:32.334
I've put in extra salt
because we've been training so hard.

12:32.418 --> 12:34.503
Thanks for waiting, everyone.

12:34.587 --> 12:35.671
Enjoy!

12:39.008 --> 12:40.676
So delicious!

12:40.801 --> 12:42.678
It really hits the spot.

12:42.761 --> 12:44.597
Yup, it's tasty.

12:44.680 --> 12:47.808
I realized something during this training.

12:47.892 --> 12:51.270
The reason why most of the
current Hashiras don't have Tsugukos.

12:51.353 --> 12:52.438
And why is that?

12:52.521 --> 12:55.024
I think I figured it out too.

12:55.107 --> 12:57.902
It's too harsh, so everyone runs away.

12:57.985 --> 12:59.028
Yeah.

12:59.111 --> 13:01.655
For example, look at that Blonde Guy.

13:01.739 --> 13:05.493
The difference in ability with Hashira
struck him and broke his spirit.

13:05.576 --> 13:08.871
The Hashira can handle things like this
as if it's nothing.

13:08.954 --> 13:11.540
They're truly amazing.

13:11.624 --> 13:13.626
I agree.

13:13.709 --> 13:16.670
You're really good at cooking rice,
aren't you?

13:16.754 --> 13:17.922
It's delicious!

13:18.005 --> 13:20.883
True, and good at grilling fish too.

13:20.966 --> 13:23.052
I'm the son of
a charcoal burner after all.

13:23.135 --> 13:23.969
SMUG!

13:24.053 --> 13:25.095
That makes sense!

13:25.179 --> 13:26.764
Cooking is all about the heat.

13:28.140 --> 13:30.309
Grilled onigiris are also delicious.

13:31.685 --> 13:33.187
Nice job, Tanjiro.

13:34.230 --> 13:35.731
Eat as much as you like.

13:37.107 --> 13:40.110
The taste is even more perfect
thanks to the miso sauce.

13:40.194 --> 13:41.570
It's making me tear up.

13:41.654 --> 13:44.031
I get it. It's like it was made by Mom.

13:44.114 --> 13:45.533
Yeah, yeah.

13:46.242 --> 13:47.576
Mother!

13:47.660 --> 13:49.078
Mom!

13:50.037 --> 13:51.038
It feels…

13:52.039 --> 13:53.541
a bit nostalgic.

14:09.723 --> 14:11.475
Wa… Water…

14:14.311 --> 14:16.480
I couldn't do it today either.

14:16.564 --> 14:19.024
It's already the sixth day.
What should I do?

14:19.108 --> 14:22.736
We don't know how long
the demons will remain quiet.

14:22.820 --> 14:24.196
I need to hurry.

14:25.155 --> 14:27.741
Is it because I lack physical strength?

14:28.450 --> 14:30.828
Or is there another breathing method?

14:31.745 --> 14:36.208
I've been training a lot,
but I still can't maintain the mark.

14:38.085 --> 14:41.213
Is the mark on your forehead
getting darker?

14:41.297 --> 14:43.549
Genya? Are you all right?

14:43.632 --> 14:47.469
After that incident, I was worried
because I couldn't get in touch with you.

14:47.553 --> 14:49.305
I was under house arrest.

14:49.388 --> 14:51.515
I got scolded by Himejima.

14:52.850 --> 14:55.853
Even though I was told
not to meet my brother,

14:55.936 --> 14:57.521
things ended up like that.

15:03.193 --> 15:04.445
I see.

15:04.528 --> 15:06.405
Sorry for getting you involved.

15:07.031 --> 15:08.741
And thanks for protecting me.

15:08.824 --> 15:10.409
No need.

15:10.492 --> 15:12.912
Anyway, about your mark.

15:12.995 --> 15:15.748
-Oh! Is it getting darker?
-Yup.

15:15.831 --> 15:18.375
No one told me.

15:18.459 --> 15:21.879
These people see you every day.
No wonder they didn't notice it.

15:21.962 --> 15:24.173
-Do you have a mirror?
-No.

15:24.256 --> 15:26.008
I'll lend you mine later.

15:28.093 --> 15:29.762
Is it really getting darker?

15:30.471 --> 15:32.848
That's great then. I'm glad.

15:32.932 --> 15:34.016
Go die!

15:34.099 --> 15:36.143
No, you!

15:36.226 --> 15:39.438
You're training to push the boulder?
I'm doing it too.

15:40.022 --> 15:42.566
But I can't move it at all.

15:42.650 --> 15:44.443
Have you moved it?

15:44.526 --> 15:45.653
Yeah.

15:45.736 --> 15:46.779
Huh?

15:46.862 --> 15:50.658
-Are you guys doing Repetitive Action?
-What?

15:51.951 --> 15:53.661
I see, you aren't.

15:54.203 --> 15:56.997
That's because Himejima
isn't good at teaching.

15:57.081 --> 15:59.708
You have to watch him carefully
and learn his skills.

16:00.376 --> 16:03.045
To heighten concentration
to the utmost limit,

16:03.128 --> 16:05.881
you must perform
predetermined actions in advance.

16:05.965 --> 16:08.467
In my case, I chant Nembutsu.

16:08.550 --> 16:10.260
Himejima does the same!

16:10.344 --> 16:12.596
Right! He always mutters,
"Namu Namu," right?

16:13.347 --> 16:14.515
Namu…

16:15.349 --> 16:16.392
Adios!

16:16.475 --> 16:18.060
Don't come again!

16:18.143 --> 16:19.311
See you!

16:19.395 --> 16:21.605
Thank you, Genya. I'll try that.

16:21.689 --> 16:23.399
Don't push yourself too hard.

16:24.358 --> 16:27.569
Even if I say that,
he's not the type to listen.

16:30.614 --> 16:32.324
Let's try it once more.

16:42.835 --> 16:44.128
Repetitive Action.

16:45.045 --> 16:47.131
Remember what Genya said.

16:48.674 --> 16:51.593
Doing it will open all your senses.

16:51.677 --> 16:55.389
According to Himejima, even though
I can't use breathing techniques,

16:55.472 --> 16:59.309
if I use Repetitive Action,
I can move the boulder.

17:00.144 --> 17:02.980
But I still have a long way to go.

17:09.987 --> 17:12.406
When they use this technique,

17:12.990 --> 17:15.868
Himejima and Genya
recall memories of anger and pain.

17:15.951 --> 17:19.496
It increases their heart rate
and body temperature.

17:27.546 --> 17:30.090
Damn it. Still can't move it.

17:30.174 --> 17:31.592
Tanjiro!

17:32.593 --> 17:34.678
Hurry up and make dinner!

17:34.762 --> 17:39.183
We've already tasted yours,
we won't be able to eat anyone else's.

17:39.266 --> 17:40.934
Is it already dinner time?

17:41.685 --> 17:42.936
I'll be there.

17:43.020 --> 17:44.396
Yo! Our mother!

17:44.480 --> 17:45.773
Our mother!

17:49.777 --> 17:51.028
Welcome back, Genya.

17:51.779 --> 17:52.988
I'll help you.

17:53.072 --> 17:54.281
Thank you.

17:55.991 --> 17:57.076
How was it?

17:57.159 --> 17:59.453
Were you able to do Repetitive Action?

18:00.954 --> 18:03.540
It feels different
from Total Concentration.

18:04.124 --> 18:06.752
It's likely to stir up emotions.

18:07.586 --> 18:08.712
Yeah.

18:08.796 --> 18:10.881
But I was thinking,

18:10.964 --> 18:16.136
maybe your forehead mark
is in a similar condition.

18:17.179 --> 18:21.934
But, Genya, Himejima and you
don't have marks like mine.

18:22.017 --> 18:24.144
That's true.

18:28.107 --> 18:29.358
Tanjiro.

18:30.234 --> 18:34.571
When do you feel your emotions strongly?

18:35.948 --> 18:37.032
Well…

18:42.704 --> 18:46.291
I'm not sure, but did I make you
remember something sad?

18:46.375 --> 18:47.668
I'm sorry.

18:50.379 --> 18:52.297
I believe you can do it.

18:52.381 --> 18:53.590
Thank you.

19:05.978 --> 19:08.147
By performing Repetitive Action,

19:08.230 --> 19:12.192
I can instantly heighten my concentration
to the utmost limit at any time.

19:13.026 --> 19:18.282
My Repetitive Action begins with
imagining the faces of my loved ones.

19:20.117 --> 19:24.454
Then, recalling Rengoku's words.

19:25.789 --> 19:27.541
"Set your heart ablaze."

19:43.015 --> 19:48.270
I hope I can manifest this state
of darker mark longer.

19:49.563 --> 19:51.315
Oh! Gonpachiro!

19:51.398 --> 19:56.153
He even starts training
at this hour before dawn.

19:56.236 --> 19:58.739
His stamina might not last a day.

19:58.822 --> 20:00.908
I won't lose to him!

20:12.085 --> 20:14.671
I couldn't do it at first, but…

20:19.051 --> 20:21.803
Now exert my full strength
from Repetitive Action.

20:22.429 --> 20:24.014
Over and over again.

20:24.848 --> 20:27.267
As I repeated them,

20:29.645 --> 20:31.605
my body started to remember.

20:33.523 --> 20:38.153
Remember the process of exerting
full strength from Repetitive Action!

20:41.949 --> 20:43.533
-For real?
-Seriously?

20:59.883 --> 21:02.886
He did it! Tanjiro pushed the boulder!

21:02.970 --> 21:05.222
Shit! He beat me!

21:05.305 --> 21:07.182
He's a monster.

21:20.153 --> 21:23.198
What is he plotting?

21:25.117 --> 21:28.453
Now, what am I going to do?

21:29.913 --> 21:34.835
What do you look like, Ubuyashiki?

21:42.009 --> 21:46.305
The flame that burns heaven

21:46.388 --> 21:53.353
Truer than the truth

21:53.437 --> 21:57.399
The voice of prayers and
The sounds of shouting

21:57.482 --> 22:04.031
Are fleeting like winged insects

22:04.114 --> 22:08.660
Why do those who devour lives

22:08.744 --> 22:15.625
Beg mercy as if not knowing impurity

22:15.709 --> 22:21.798
Those souls that win through
The darkness can only reach

22:21.882 --> 22:26.595
Obtain that eternity

22:26.678 --> 22:32.309
There's a feeling here
That doesn't know demise

22:32.392 --> 22:37.606
Speak your dream, you strong one

22:37.689 --> 22:43.278
A resound congratulating tune of eternity

22:43.361 --> 22:49.034
Into the light that governs the sky

22:49.117 --> 22:53.246
In the corner of the world that is messy

22:53.330 --> 22:57.584
A blade of a sword
That still wriggles and resists

22:57.667 --> 23:03.590
Grovels and struggles miserably

23:06.009 --> 23:07.010
DEMON SLAYER: KIMETSU NO YAIBA:
HASHIRA TRAINING ARC NO. 6

23:07.594 --> 23:10.263
This time I'll tell you about Himejima.

23:12.057 --> 23:14.059
What's wrong, Himejima?

23:17.020 --> 23:18.396
What a happy family.

23:18.480 --> 23:19.606
Huh?

23:20.524 --> 23:23.443
It's time for the Taisho period secret.

23:23.527 --> 23:25.987
Himejima cries easily.

23:26.071 --> 23:29.574
It seems he cries just from
seeing litter scattered around.

23:32.994 --> 23:37.624
Namu… Cats are cute. Namu… Cats are cute.

23:38.458 --> 23:39.876
Look, he's crying again.

23:40.877 --> 23:44.840
Next up on Episode 7:
"Gyomei Himejima the Stone Hashira"

23:44.923 --> 23:46.007
TO BE CONTINUED
